Let clients download an original upload from the files_settings backend with
GET /v1/files/{file_id}/content?raw=true.

files-api returns the content it extracted from an upload by default and the
upload itself with `raw`. The parameter is files-api's, not OpenAI's, so this is
not an upstream bug. The proxy drops every query parameter but `provider`, and
FileContentRequest has no extra_query, so `raw` never reaches the backend.

Forward `raw`, and no other parameter, as extra_query to the OpenAI SDK's
files.content(). Without `raw`, nothing changes.

Checks: raw content check in tests/verify_files_settings.py

